{"note":"Dengue in Paraguay. Values are reported cases (suspected + probable + confirmed, i.e. notifications; not only laboratory-confirmed). DEPARTMENT LEVEL ('yearly', 'monthly'): 2019-01 to 2023-12 only, for the 17 departments plus the capital district Asuncion. OpenDengue has no sub-national data for Paraguay, so these come from a third-party open transcription of the weekly arbovirus bulletins of DGVS (Ministry of Health): Care99/dengue-cluster v1.0.0 on Zenodo, which publishes weekly incidence per 100,000 (classification 'TOTAL'). Case counts were recovered exactly as incidence x denominator / 100,000: every value is an integer multiple of one case, and the department counts add up to the dataset's national row in all weeks. Epidemiological weeks (Sunday to Saturday) are assigned to the month and year in which the week starts; the two edge weeks falling in incomplete months were dropped. The series ends in mid-January 2024, so its last weeks were probably still being updated: the week starting 2023-12-31 (counted in 2023-12) is about 40% below the figure PAHO later published. The 2013 and 2024 epidemics are NOT covered at department level (no open machine-readable source found: DGVS publishes PDF bulletins only). NATIONAL LEVEL: 'national' = annual totals 1980-2024 as reported to PAHO, from OpenDengue V1.3.1 (zeros before 1999 are as published and may mean 'not reported'); 'national_monthly' = OpenDengue weekly national counts 2015-10 to 2024-11 aggregated by week start, complete months only (so 12 months do not add up exactly to the PAHO epidemiological-year total). The two sources do not match exactly: for 2020-2023 the department totals are 4% to 23% below PAHO's weekly totals, but for 2019 they are 2.3 times higher (38,345 vs 16,333), which points to a different case definition in what was reported to PAHO that year. Reporting rules and case definitions changed over the years, so compare magnitudes and timing, not small differences. 'lat'/'lon' = geometric centroid of the department polygon (geoBoundaries gbOpen PRY ADM1, not the capital city). 'pop' = resident population, INE Paraguay, 2022 National Census, final results. 'pop_src' = denominator used by the source dataset for its incidence rates (consistent with INE's 2015-revision projection for 2023, which is about 24% above the 2022 census count).","source":{"name":"Care99/dengue-cluster (C. Rodas), csv/casos.csv: weekly dengue incidence by department, transcribed from DGVS/MSPBS Paraguay arbovirus bulletins","url":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18423650","version":"v1.0.0 (2026-01-29)","licence":"CC BY 4.0","original":"Dirección General de Vigilancia de la Salud (DGVS), MSPBS Paraguay, https://dgvs.mspbs.gov.py/arbovirosis/"},"source_national":{"name":"OpenDengue (national extract of PAHO/WHO reports), Clarke J. et al., Scientific Data 2024","url":"https://opendengue.org/data.html","version":"V1.3.1 (Temporal extract)","licence":"CC BY 4.0"},"source_population":{"name":"INE Paraguay, Censo Nacional de Población y Viviendas 2022, resultados finales, Cuadro 1","url":"https://www.ine.gov.py/censo2022/","year":2022},"source_centroids":{"name":"geoBoundaries gbOpen PRY ADM1 (boundaries: DGEEC 2012)","url":"https://www.geoboundaries.org/","licence":"CC BY 4.0"},"coverage":{"departments":["2019-01","2023-12"],"national":[1980,2024],"national_monthly":["2015-10","2024-11"]},"departments":[{"id":"PY-ASU","name":"Asunción","lat":-25.291,"lon":-57.605,"pop":462241,"pop_src":521091},{"id":"PY-1","name":"Concepción","lat":-22.84,"lon":-57.11,"pop":206181,"pop_src":266072},{"id":"PY-2","name":"San Pedro","lat":-24.177,"lon":-56.631,"pop":355175,"pop_src":450802},{"id":"PY-3","name":"Cordillera","lat":-25.211,"lon":-56.962,"pop":268037,"pop_src":323040},{"id":"PY-4","name":"Guairá","lat":-25.831,"lon":-56.301,"pop":179555,"pop_src":234920},{"id":"PY-5","name":"Caaguazú","lat":-25.2,"lon":-55.886,"pop":431519,"pop_src":582630},{"id":"PY-6","name":"Caazapá","lat":-26.242,"lon":